# What a build uploads to the daemon before a single instruction runs.
#
# The syntax here is not .gitignore's, and that is the trap this file is
# written around. A .gitignore pattern with no slash in it matches at
# every depth, so `*.log` there reaches a log twelve directories down. A
# .dockerignore pattern is matched against the whole relative path with
# Go's filepath.Match, whose `*` never crosses a separator, so `*.log`
# here means "a log in the context root" and nothing below it. The two
# files sit side by side and read as one vocabulary; only one of them
# means what it appears to.
#
# So every exclusion below carries the `**/` prefix, which covers the
# context root as well as every directory under it. There is no bare
# name here to read as reaching the whole tree while covering one
# directory of it, and no judgment call about which patterns were meant
# to reach: they all do. test/layer-2-integration/build-context.test.js
# holds that by planting a file for every pattern in this file, at the
# root and one directory in, and rendering the result with docker, so
# what is asserted is where a file ends up rather than what a line says.
#
# The last line that matches a path decides it, which is what the
# re-include at the end of this file depends on.

# Version control and CI definitions.
**/.git
**/.github
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes

# Editor, OS and assistant scratch.
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.claude
**/.playwright-mcp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini

# Maintainer-local notes and internal specs. Nothing in the build reads
# them and they are not written for anyone running this server.
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/memory

# Dependency and build output. Nothing is resolved from a registry at
# build time: the framework is vendored in the tree and ships with it, so
# a dependency directory in the context is a developer's local install.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/public/dist

# Registry configuration. The build installs nothing, and this file is
# where a registry credential lives when one exists.
**/.npmrc

# Runtime state. A data directory holds live mail, account credentials and
# sealed DKIM private keys, whether it sits at the container path or at a
# developer's local override.
**/data
**/data-e2e
**/blobs
**/queue
**/tlsrpt
**/tls
**/acme
**/var
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm

# Test fixtures, and the diagnostics the gates persist. A gate log carries
# captured source and whole failure transcripts.
**/test
**/.test-output
**/*.log
**/*.pid
**/*.pid.lock

# The fuzz harnesses, their seed corpora and the ClusterFuzzLite build
# definition. Nothing in the image reads them: the Dockerfile copies bin,
# lib and docs by name, and the harnesses run against the tree in CI
# rather than against the image. A seed corpus also grows without bound
# during a local run, because libFuzzer writes every input it keeps back
# into the seed directory.
**/fuzz
**/.clusterfuzzlite

# The reproducer a fuzz run writes when it finds something. libFuzzer puts
# it in the directory the run started from, which for the documented
# command is the context root.
**/crash-*
**/leak-*
**/timeout-*
**/oom-*
**/slow-unit-*

# Credential and secret material, excluded at every depth rather than in
# the context root alone.
#
# .env is named because the compose stack reads the vault passphrase from
# the environment and documents a local build from this same directory in
# the same file. An operator who follows both halves has the passphrase
# that seals every key on their data volume sitting in the context root.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cert
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/secrets.json
**/credentials.json
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*

# Backup and patch artifacts.
**/*.bak
**/*.orig
**/*.rej

# The vendored framework is what the image is built from, and one rule
# above reaches into it: it carries a trust anchor whose extension is on
# the credential list. An image built without that file ships a vendored
# tree that no longer matches the one lib/vendor/MANIFEST.json pins, which
# breaks the integrity check for everyone who did not vendor it
# themselves. This must stay last, because the last matching line wins.
#
# It names the certificate shape rather than the subtree, and the
# difference is the whole point of the line. The last matching line
# decides a path, so a re-include written as `lib/vendor/**` does not
# restore one anchor: it cancels every exclusion above it for everything
# under that prefix, and the environment file, private key, registry
# configuration and database withheld everywhere else are uploaded from
# there. The Dockerfile copies `lib` whole into the runtime stage, so
# those do not stop at the daemon: they ship inside the image.
!lib/vendor/**/*.pem
